- `SpawnListInput.status` still accepts `queued` and `finalizing` on the extension and MCP
  surfaces, while `spawn list` rejects them as filters. Those surfaces never
  warned about the values, so deprecate them there for one release before rejecting them.
- `work_sessions.py` builds its active chat set from any active session attached to
  the work item, which is wider than `spawn_work_id` (active primaries plus
  recorded child work ids): a child session that switches items still counts.
  The wider rule is `work sessions`' existing behavior, so folding it into the
  shared membership helper would change that command. Decide which rule is right.
- Per-work commands remain slow after the spawn read was indexed: `active_session_work_ids`
  replays the 98 MB `sessions.jsonl` (~59k events) on every call (~200-365 ms), and
  `work_session_chat_ids` plus the index's `sessions()` take about 0.9 s. Cache or
  narrow the session read rather than adding another parallel fast path.
